# ============================================================================
# NOTE ON CLEANUP
# No PATH-= lines are needed for Scoop directories: --admin-setenv sweeps every
# Machine PATH entry inside apps\, shims\, persist\, global\ before this file is
# applied, and --clean-user-scope does the same for the User PATH. Use PATH-= only
# for entries outside those directories that you want gone.
#
# $NAME is expanded when the line is applied. A name defined anywhere in this
# file (or in a user.* file, for User scope) resolves to that definition, whatever
# the order of the lines; other names come from the registry. Write $$ for a
# literal dollar sign (PROMPT=$$P$$G).
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# BASE DIRECTORIES
# USR is the Scoop root (same as $SCOOP), DATA holds project data and optional
# caches (see the end of the file), DEVL_ROOT the source trees. TMP/TEMP must be
# short and without spaces: Scoop and several installers fail on long or
# redirected temp paths.
# ============================================================================
USR=C:\usr
DATA=C:\data
DEVL_ROOT=C:\devl
TMP=C:\tmp
TEMP=C:\tmp

# ============================================================================
# GIT (installed by the bootstrap) and OpenSSH
# NOTE: every PATH+= line lands in front of C:\Windows\System32. Git's usr\bin
# holds extensionless files (cmd, notepad, find, sort) that PowerShell then
# resolves instead of the Windows programs, which opens a "select an app" dialog
# or runs the Unix tool. If that bites you, use PATH=+ (append) for the usr\bin
# line so that System32 stays in front; scoop-boot itself calls cmd.exe and
# notepad.exe by full path for this reason.
# ============================================================================
GIT_HOME=$USR\apps\git\current
PATH+=$GIT_HOME\mingw64\bin
PATH+=$GIT_HOME\usr\bin
PATH+=$GIT_HOME\cmd
GIT_SSH=$USR\apps\openssh\current\ssh.exe

# ============================================================================
# LOCALE & ENCODING
# ============================================================================
LANG=en_US.UTF-8
LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8
LANGUAGE=en_US:en
